5,1,1,talk,Servas,,We must learn from past mistakes. I will examine the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I’m worried about where the money actually comes from. I’ll look into the capital budget and software allowance.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Sakura,,"Ooh, I bet the network at customer plants is tricky! I’ll check that and in-house developer availability.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I will examine the time lost to copying existing records and the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I will examine the staffing of the coordination group and the handling of vendor queries.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"A pattern should be visible by now. I am curious to see if the narrow tools truly survived their first year, as the reviews suggest.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,I just want to make sure the recurring costs are actually covered. It’s hard to plan if the budget is frozen.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"I hope the developers aren’t too busy! If they’re stuck on the accounting upgrade, that’s a huge red flag for our timeline.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I need to see if the daily friction is real. If we lose an hour copying data, that effort must be weighed against the proposal’s promise.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"I need to verify if the coordination group is actually understaffed. If two people handle all logs, that workload is unsustainable and will break under any new proposal.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, a frozen capital line is a hard boundary. Yet, if the recurring allowance remains open, we might still find a path forward.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, yes, that’s right. If the capital line is frozen, we have to rely on the software allowance. I just need to confirm it’s enough.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, if copying records eats an hour daily, that’s a huge waste! I’m hoping my network checks reveal why the groundwork always fails.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
